{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex"},"metadata":{"title":"Regex","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"class","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Regex"}],"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Regex","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:4GLib5RegexC","roleHeading":"Class"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Regex"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"After instantiating a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"type":"text","text":", you can use its methods to find matches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in a string, replace matches within a string, or split the string at matches."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"text":" implements regular expression pattern matching using syntax and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"semantics (such as character classes, quantifiers, and capture groups)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"similar to Perl regular expression. See the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"man:pcre2pattern(3)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for details."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A typical scenario for regex pattern matching is to check if a string"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"matches a pattern. The following statements implement this scenario.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"{ .c }","code":["const char *regex_pattern = \".*GLib.*\";","const char *string_to_search = \"You will love the GLib implementation of regex\";","`g_autoptr(GMatchInfo)` match_info = NULL;","`g_autoptr(GRegex)` regex = NULL;","","regex = g_regex_new (regex_pattern, G_REGEX_DEFAULT, G_REGEX_MATCH_DEFAULT, NULL);","g_assert (regex != NULL);","","if (g_regex_match (regex, string_to_search, G_REGEX_MATCH_DEFAULT, &match_info))","  {","    int start_pos, end_pos;","    g_match_info_fetch_pos (match_info, 0, &start_pos, &end_pos);","    g_print (\"Match successful! Overall pattern matches bytes `d` to `d`\\n\", start_pos, end_pos);","  }","else","  {","    g_print (\"No match!\\n\");","  }"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The constructor for ","type":"text"},{"code":"GRegex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" includes two sets of bitmapped flags:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"[flags","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexCompileFlags"},{"type":"text","text":"]—These flags"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"control how GLib compiles the regex. There are options for case"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"sensitivity, multiline, ignoring whitespace, etc."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[flags"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexMatchFlags","isActive":true},{"text":"]—These flags control","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"GRegex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s matching behavior, such as anchoring and customizing definitions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for newline characters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some regex patterns include backslash assertions, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\d"},{"text":" (digit) or","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\\D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (non-digit). The regex pattern must escape those backslashes. For","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example, the pattern "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"\\\\d\\\\D\""},{"type":"text","text":" matches a digit followed by a non-digit."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"GLib’s implementation of pattern matching includes a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start_position"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"argument for some of the match, replace, and split methods. Specifying","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"a start position provides flexibility when you want to ignore the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" characters of a string, but want to incorporate backslash assertions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"at character "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" - 1. For example, a database field contains inconsistent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spelling for a job title: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"healthcare provider"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"health-care provider","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The database manager wants to make the spelling consistent by adding a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"hyphen when it is missing. The following regex pattern tests for the string"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"care","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" preceded by a non-word boundary character (instead of a hyphen)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and followed by a space.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["const char *regex_pattern = \"\\\\Bcare\\\\s\";"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"{ .c }"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An efficient way to match with this pattern is to start examining at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start_position"},{"text":" 6 in the string ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"healthcare"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"health-care","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"{ .c }","type":"codeListing","code":["const char *regex_pattern = \"\\\\Bcare\\\\s\";","const char *string_to_search = \"healthcare provider\";","`g_autoptr(GMatchInfo)` match_info = NULL;","`g_autoptr(GRegex)` regex = NULL;","","regex = g_regex_new (","  regex_pattern,","  G_REGEX_DEFAULT,","  G_REGEX_MATCH_DEFAULT,","  NULL);","g_assert (regex != NULL);","","g_regex_match_full (","  regex,","  string_to_search,","  -1,","  6, \/\/ position of 'c' in the test string.","  G_REGEX_MATCH_DEFAULT,","  &match_info,","  NULL);"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The method [method","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.Regex.match_full","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] (and other methods implementing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start_pos"},{"text":") allow for lookback before the start position to determine if","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the previous character satisfies an assertion."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unless you set the [flags"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.RegexCompileFlags.RAW"},{"type":"text","text":"] as one of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"GRegexCompileFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", all the strings passed to ","type":"text"},{"code":"GRegex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" methods must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be encoded in UTF-8. The lengths and the positions inside the strings are"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"in bytes and not in characters, so, for instance, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\xc3\\xa0"},{"type":"text","text":" (i.e., "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"à"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is two bytes long but it is treated as a single character. If you set"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G_REGEX_RAW"},{"text":", the strings can be non-valid UTF-8 strings and a byte is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"treated as a character, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\xc3\\xa0"},{"type":"text","text":" is two bytes and two characters long."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Regarding line endings, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\n"},{"text":" matches a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\n"},{"text":" character, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\r"},{"text":" matches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\r"},{"type":"text","text":" character. More generally, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\R"},{"type":"text","text":" matches all typical line endings:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"CR + LF ("},{"code":"\\r\\n","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), LF (linefeed, U+000A, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\n"},{"text":"), VT (vertical tab, U+000B,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\v"},{"text":"), FF (formfeed, U+000C, ","type":"text"},{"code":"\\f","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), CR (carriage return, U+000D, ","type":"text"},{"code":"\\r","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"NEL (next line, U+0085), LS (line separator, U+2028), and PS (paragraph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"separator, U+2029)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The behaviour of the dot, circumflex, and dollar metacharacters are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"affected by newline characters. By default, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"type":"text","text":" matches any newline"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"character matched by ","type":"text"},{"code":"\\R","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". You can limit the matched newline characters by","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifying the [flags"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_CR"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[flags","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_LF","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[flags"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_CRLF"},{"type":"text","text":"] compile options, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with [flags"},{"code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_ANY","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[flags"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_CR"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[flags","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_LF"},{"type":"text","text":"] and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[flags"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_CRLF"},{"type":"text","text":"] match options."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"These settings are also relevant when compiling a pattern if","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[flags","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.RegexCompileFlags.EXTENDED"},{"type":"text","text":"] is set and an unescaped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#"},{"text":" outside a character class is encountered. This indicates a comment","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that lasts until after the next newline."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because ","type":"text"},{"code":"GRegex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not modify its internal state between creation and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destruction, you can create and modify the same "},{"code":"GRegex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance from","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different threads. In contrast, [struct"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MatchInfo"},{"type":"text","text":"] is not thread safe."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The regular expression low-level functionalities are obtained through","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the excellent ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"http:\/\/www.pcre.org\/"},{"type":"text","text":" library written by Philip Hazel."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex"},{"type":"text","text":" type acts as a reference-counted owner of an underlying "},{"code":"GRegex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It provides the methods that can operate on this data type through ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexProtocol","isActive":true},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex"},{"type":"text","text":" as a strong reference or owner of a "},{"code":"GRegex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (instead of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex","isActive":true},{"text":") for a lightweight Swift reference to an underlying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(_:)-14i11","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(_:)-38s23","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(_:)-5mtur","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(_:)-7dwt1","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(_:)-8o1r7","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(cPointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(gconstpointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(gpointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(opaquePointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(pattern:compileOptions:matchOptions:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(raw:)-1y1qf","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(raw:)-4klw6","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(retaining:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(retainingCPointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(retainingOpaquePointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(retainingRaw:)-1u2ye","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/init(retainingRaw:)-7yto8"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/ptr"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex\/RegexProtocol-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexProtocol"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/docume